hem up  and then i just have this wonderful dirt  here  and then next i'm gonna put on some  grass and what i did for that is i just  took some coconut  and then put some green food coloring in  it and just mixed it up with my hands  and you get this cool grass  so we'll put our grass on there  then we're going to make it a graveyard  now and of course with a graveyard you  need to have tombstones right so what i  did is i went to a craft store and i  found these cool little edible  tombstones you could use those if you  wanted to  or you can make them by yourself so i  got some cookie dough some  sugar cookie dough  just the tube stuff and but make sure to  bake them first and then cut them into  the tombstone shape or else they won't  work so we'll do that i also found some  of course gummy worms right gotta have  gum worms  going in and out of there  and then i have some ghosts what's a  graveyard without ghosts and some  spiders  anyways you get the point right just  have fun with this stuff kids get  involved and of course they're gonna  want to eat it too  we'll put one more tombstone in there  one more spider  and that is our  lovely graveyard that dirt pudding  awesome  you can put this back in the fridge if  you wanted to or you could just serve it  right away if you're not going to serve  right away definitely put it in the  fridge and then it will kind of set up  for you and look nice and everything so  but anyways the point is to have fun  with your food at halloween you can find  all of these ingredients at your local  smiths thank you so much for watching  thank you for shopping we'll see you all  next time bye everybody thank you to  smith's food and drug for sponsoring  this segment for the full recipe  ingredients and more visit  smithsfoodanddrug.com
 

